verses.text:
Whatever was, will be again,
whatever was done will be done once more;
nothing is new beneath the sun.

Whatever is, has already been,
and what will be has already been,
and God seeks out what has been driven away.{d}

For like the crackle of thorns under a pot,{b}
so is the laughter of the fool.
This too is a breath.

When the ax is dull and its blade is left unsharpened,
one has to swing harder;
but wisdom gives the edge that succeeds.

Do not curse the king even in your private thoughts,{d}
and do not curse the wealthy even where you sleep,
for some bird of the skies will carry the sound,
some winged thing will tell the tale.

Rejoice, young man, while you are young;
let your heart be glad in your early years.
Walk where your heart leads
and after what your eyes behold,{b}
but know that over all these things
God will call you to account.

before the sun and the light,
the moon and the stars grow dark,
and the clouds return after the rain;

when heights are frightening
and dangers lurk along the way;
when the almond is in flower,{c}
the locust is weighed down,
and desire fails as the caper berry{d} does;
because the human goes to his eternal home,
and the mourners go about in the street;
